# Environment of every sim-* container (docker/compose.yaml env_file), so every
# docker-exec'd node inherits it. It plays the role of a rover's /etc/rover/rover.env:
# RMW, domain and zenoh URIs here; per-agent identity comes from the pane commands
# (scripts/sim.py), since one container serves several agents.
#
# Same transport as JR02: rmw_zenoh_cpp on domain 22 (under zenoh the domain is only a
# key prefix). The zenoh files are mounted from docker/zenoh/ at /rover_sim/zenoh.
#
# Domain 22 is also the fleet's, so the key space alone does not keep sim traffic
# (JR81, /trajs, /exploration/return_home) apart from the real robots; the network does.
# Every sim container is on the internal network rover-sim only, with no route off it and
# no address of the host's to reach, and sim.py refuses to start nodes unless that holds
# (scripts/sim.py check_isolation). 22 is kept for strict parity with JR02, as the plan
# decided. A sim-only domain would add a second barrier at no parity cost (parity_check
# compares params and the graph, not the domain): if wanted, change it here and record
# it in tools/reference/jr02/allowed_deviations.yaml.
RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_zenoh_cpp
ROS_DOMAIN_ID=22
ZENOH_ROUTER_CONFIG_URI=/rover_sim/zenoh/router.json5
ZENOH_SESSION_CONFIG_URI=/rover_sim/zenoh/session.json5
